  "notes": [
    "Six original editable Remotion films, with separate landscape/portrait layouts: 96 seconds and 2880 encoded frames. Each uses a single actual frame capture, not the old Forge three-exposure route.",
    "All 2880 frames independently decoded by the build checker, and 2880 actual production DOM text-bound samples measured. Each final manifest binds the same complete current 21-file source inventory.",
    "Every final film has sampled visual review of 15 encoded full-resolution frames and a sheet. Paper uses verified byte-identical rebinding to prior reviewed pixels; Citrus and Mineral R2 have fresh independent review.",
    "Chrome normal-speed automated muted playback reached ended, presenting all 480 frames per film with zero observed dropped frames. Paper binds the same R1 MP4 bytes.",
    "Human full watching and audio listening not performed. Technical, sampled visual and playback results are separate from subjective music and user aesthetic approval.",
    "GIF previews are 10fps silent reductions from final MP4s. The actual videos are 30fps with full original scores.",
    "Citrus is an original concept advertisement; mineral art is an original plant/motif animation, not a historical mural reconstruction.",
    "Original scene vectors and original procedural music; locally bundled OFL font subsets preserve source/notice records. No external model or sample provider.",
    "Earlier failed readability/pace/scale/label samples and review reports retained outside public repository. They are not current acceptance evidence.",
    "Portable inventory validation compares source/media/PCM hashes and declarations; it does not rerender, rewatch or certify aesthetics."
  ],
